# /etc/cron.d/knijka — Книжка.AI staging schedule (audit 2026-07-24, H-17).
# Install: copy to /etc/cron.d/knijka, `chown root:root`, `chmod 644`.
# cron.d files must NOT be executable and must name the user in each line.
#
# PATH matters: cron's default PATH has neither node/npm (nvm or /usr/local)
# nor pm2. A deploy that cannot find pm2 fails at the restart — with the build
# already swapped in — which is the worst place to fail. Adjust the node path
# to whatever `dirname "$(command -v node)"` prints on the box.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
HOME=/root
MAILTO=""

# Every 5 minutes: deploy the newest CI-green commit, if there is a new one.
# Ticks where nothing changed are silent, so the log only ever shows real work.
*/5 * * * * root /opt/knijka/autodeploy.sh >> /var/log/knijka-autodeploy.log 2>&1

# 03:15 UTC daily: verified database dump. Sunday's is kept for 8 weeks.
# Deploys also take one immediately before every migration — this is the
# safety net for the days when nobody deploys at all.
#
# ⚠ THE PATH BELOW WAS WRONG UNTIL 2026-08-28, and the way it was wrong is the
# point. It read `/opt/knijka/backup-db.sh`; the script is at
# `/opt/knijka/tools/deploy/backup-db.sh`. Installed exactly as written, cron
# would have run a file that does not exist, every night, for ever — and a
# backup job that fails silently is indistinguishable from one that works
# until the day you reach for a dump. Checked on the box: `/var/backups/knijka`
# did not exist, no `*.dump` existed anywhere on the VPS, and the company had
# ZERO database backups.
#
# ⚠ AND THIS FILE IS NOT WHAT THE VPS ACTUALLY USES. The staging box runs
# autodeploy from a SYSTEMD TIMER (`knijka-autodeploy.timer`, OnUnitActiveSec
# 300), not from cron — so installing the autodeploy line above would deploy
# twice. The backup now runs the same way, `knijka-backup.timer` at 03:15 UTC,
# installed and proved on 2026-08-28 (Result=success, dump written, verified,
# retention applied). Keep this file as the portable recipe for a box without
# systemd; on the staging VPS, the timers are the truth.
15 3 * * * root /bin/bash /opt/knijka/tools/deploy/backup-db.sh scheduled >> /var/log/knijka-backup.log 2>&1
